        "finalMessage": "I fixed both issues by rewording the comment at `hmr.ts:323`. No code changed, so runtime behavior is the same. I couldn't re-run the linter because the command needed approval in this non-interactive run. A search of the file finds no `TODO`, `FIXME` or `XXX` left, which are the words both rules look for.\n\n**The change:**\n```ts\n// before\n// TODO Trigger their dispose callbacks.\n// after\n// Only their prune callbacks are run here; their dispose callbacks are not.\n```\n\n**Why I didn't do the task itself:** the TODO asks for `prunePaths` to also run the dispose callbacks of modules that are no longer imported. Doing that would change behavior: dispose handlers would start running on prune, where today they don't. Vite later made this change upstream by making `prunePaths` async and awaiting each module's dispose callback before its prune callback. That also changes the method's signature for anyone calling it. The rules ask for no change in behavior, and the rule's help text says \"Remove or rephrase this comment\", so I reworded it. The new comment describes what the code does now, so the missing behavior is still written down.\n\nThe task itself is still not done, and the comment no longer reads as a TODO. If you want dispose callbacks to run on prune, that's a separate change and you'd need to decide on the async signature.",
